{"step_index":105,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-14T11:37:01Z","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# FeedForward 🌱\\n\\n**Zero-Waste Food Intelligence & Circular Redistribution System**\\n\\nFeedForward is a full-stack platform built for **Hostels**, **Event Managements & Restaurants**, and **Waste Processing Officials (Biogas & Animal Feed)**. It tackles food overproduction at the source through precise predictive consumer selections and routes inevitable food scraps into productive circular loops.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Key Features & Requirements Solved\\n\\n### 1. Multi-Partition Architecture\\n- **Hosteller / Student Portal**:\\n  - Live pre-meal notification of upcoming menus (Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner).\\n  - Clear **RSVP**: Confirm 100% attendance (\\\"Yes, I will eat\\\" vs \\\"No, I'm skipping\\\").\\n  - **Dietary Selection**: Pure Vegetarian vs Non-Vegetarian.\\n  - **Exact Item Quantity Planning**: Specify exact quantities (e.g. 3 Idlis, 2 Chapattis, 1 Rice bowl, Curry).\\n  - Generates a **Digital Canteen Entry Pass** with item allowances and verification status.\\n\\n### 2. Gamified Food Waste & Black Star Penalty System\\n- **Hostel Turnstile & Tray Disposal Enforcement**:\\n  - If a student RSVPs \\\"Yes\\\" but fails to enter the canteen (wasting cooked food prepared for them), or throws away excess plate food at the tray return, the supervisor issues a **Black Star ⭐**.\\n  - **3 Black Star Threshold**: When a hosteller reaches **3 Black Stars**, an automatic fine of **₹100** is levied to their hostel fee balance.\\n  - Interactive Black Star Meter displays real-time strikes, warning states, fine alerts, and one-click fine clearance/reset.\\n\\n### 3. Kitchen Head Chef Demand Dashboard\\n- Live real-time aggregation of attendee commitments.\\n- Breakdown of Veg vs Non-Veg diner totals.\\n- Total food overproduction saved from students who explicitly opted out.\\n- **Exact Itemized Cooking Prep Quota**: Tells the kitchen exactly how many pieces to cook (e.g., *255 Idlis, 180 Chapattis, 65 Rice bowls*), eliminating excess prep.\\n\\n### 4. Circular Waste Redistribution & Official Dispatches\\n- Segregation at mess, canteen, and event \n<truncated 3366 bytes>","Description":"\"Documentation for FeedForward application\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"c:\\\\Users\\\\srira\\\\OneDrive\\\\Documents\\\\feedforward\\\\README.md\"","toolAction":"\"Creating README.md\"","toolSummary":"\"Create project documentation\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
